cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "OpenQVD: A pure-Rust reader and writer for Qlik QVD files"
message: >
  If you use OpenQVD in your research, please cite it using the metadata
  below. Citation is encouraged and appreciated but not legally required.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Riley
    given-names: Nathan
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0004-1579-7312"
    website: "https://github.com/Sigilweaver"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Sigilweaver/OpenQVD"
url: "https://sigilweaver.app"
abstract: >
  OpenQVD is a standalone, cross-platform reader and writer for Qlik QVD
  (QlikView Data) files, implemented in pure Rust. Python bindings built on
  PyO3 integrate with Polars, PyArrow, and Pandas, providing schema-aware
  access to QVD's symbol-table and bit-stuffed-index storage layout without
  requiring Qlik Sense or QlikView.
license: "Apache-2.0"
